<!--
    Kundur's two-area four-machine system with a multi-terminal DC grid: complements kundur-dc.xiidm (KundurDcNetwork.create, flat).

    The machines the benchmark's (P. Kundur, Power System Stability and Control, example 12.6), on their 900 MVA: four windings, Xd
    1.8, Xq 1.7, X'd 0.3, X'q 0.55, X''d = X''q 0.25, Xl 0.2, Ra 0.0025, T'd0 8 s, T'q0 0.4 s, T''d0 0.03 s, T''q0 0.05 s, H 6.5 s
    for G1 and G2, 6.175 s for G3 and G4, no damping; its saturation Asat 0.015, Bsat 9.6, psiT1 0.9 as S(1.0) and S(1.2), the
    excess field current Asat exp(Bsat (psi - psiT1)) on psi. Its thyristor exciter, a gain of 200 behind a 10 ms transducer lag,
    the simplified AVR (a field voltage within +-5 pu, ours); its PSS, Kundur's KSTAB 20, TW 10 s, T1 0.05, T2 0.02, T3 3, T4
    5.4 s, on the speed's deviation (an output limit of 0.2 pu, ours): without it, the high-gain exciter leaves the inter-area mode
    with little or no damping. The benchmark holds its mechanical power: here each machine on a TGOV1, ours, so that the DC
    grid's droop and the load flow's small mismatches settle on a frequency - the usual data, R 5 % on 900 MW, T1 0.5 s, the
    valve within 0 and 1 pu, T2 3 s, T3 10 s, no Dt. Not a proportional governor without lag: each one a damping torque of 20 pu
    on its machine's speed, it damps the inter-area mode as much as the PSSs do (zeta 0.25 without them). With the TGOV1s, a
    fault at bus 8 (kundur-dc-fault-b8, run 2026-11-08 over 8 s): the inter-area mode at 0.6 Hz, zeta 0.04 without the PSSs,
    0.2 with them - as with no governor at all.

    The DC grid's converters averaged as CIGRE DCS2's and Ieee14DcNetwork's, a 15 % phase reactor on their rating (R 0.003 pu), DC
    capacitors of 40 ms, a bridge inductance for their blocking: CS7 and CS9 grid-following (on their DC voltage droop and DC
    voltage, as IIDM's control mode says), CSW grid-forming (a virtual synchronous machine), its island's. The wind park WTW Dynawo's
    WT4B example (ExampleNetworks.wt4bDynawoExample) on its own 200 MVA. Each DC line one lumped pi of its 400 kV conductor: 2 L
    and C / 2 of CIGRE B4's +-200 kV per-km pole data (OHL 0.8273 mH, 0.0139 uF; cable 2.615 mH, 0.2185 uF).
-->
